Greg's word, 2026-11-26 ~17:46Z, verbatim via Engram::Asistant (TermAl mailbox 588693a8 #2865), answering the joint question (Engram::Fable #2122 / Termal::Fable2 #2864): „Tak dla Engram na Window B.”

It covers, on Windows B, for Codex sessions (Engram session-12 for the Engram project, TermAl session-5 for the TermAl project):
(1) creating the local Engram store C:\Users\Greg\.engram (engram init);
(2) enabling task sync and importing tasks and memories from engram-data, by explicit export and import, not plain sync;
(3) enabling the Engram MCP integration for the Engram and TermAl projects on WinB's TermAl, as a per-project setting.

Context: Greg's earlier words „Chwila!! Powien byc engram” (#2859) and „Po to mamy sync engram. + Kimi. Dlatego robimy te toole.” (#2861). Earlier refusals that were NOT bypassed: session-8's Claude classifier ("Destructive or Unwanted Actions") and session-12's own AGENTS.md check. This word is what they asked for.
